From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shawn Hoffman <business@symbrkrs.com>
Date: Sun, 10 May 2026 21:51:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] 9188: nds32: bug fixes and ex9.it / ifc implementation

nds32 bug fixes: * sp_bound_priv,sp_base,sp_base_priv:
 fix csreg addr. * fix data endianness issues. * handle mfusr/mtusr PC
 correctly. * scw: inhibit decompiler optimizing out check. * tlbop
 Rt,Ra,Probe: indicate Rt is written. * dpref: fix shift amount. * cctl:
 indicate Rt may be written. * standby: allow fallthrough. * addi.gp: display
 Rt, Imm19s in disasm. * *_srli: fix shift direction. *
 bgezal/bltzal/jralnez/jrnez: fix branch polarity. * abs: fix pcode (implement
 saturation behavior). * ave: fix shift amount and don't chop off high bits. *
 clz/clo: use lzcount pcodeop instead of loop. * add_abs_diff: fix
 intermediate truncation. * add5.pc: fix addr computation. * bmski33: fix
 pcode. * pop25: fix sp calculations (pop imm5 first; use Lmwai instead of
 LmwOp). * FP ops: fix pcodeops being called; indicate that Fxt is input AND
 output. * fmtcsr: constrain to Fsa=0.

added instructions:
* mtlbi/mtlei: just set lb/le registers.
* ifcall/ifret: unimpl for now.

misc:
* push25: handle setting s2 without branch.
* add branch_if/call_if macros. should help with IFCALL support.

note:
The fixes to abs and add_abs_diff make the pcode correct, however the
decompiler output may not be ideal.

nds32: implement ex9.it/ifc

nds32: add regression tests

These tests have been distilled from problematic examples
found in real-world code.

nds32: add NDS32MT7663LoadFlowTest and real-world binaries

This commit is for reference and not intended to be merged.
However, some of the helper analyzers/scripts may be useful
enough to be merged.
